      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-133640",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/fe/fed9612081dee292f36784382220462a18a5afa696f39c85205e4410b1080156.png)\n\nThe mass $M$, in grams, of a radioactive isotope after $t$ years can be modeled using the exponential function $M(t) = ab^{t}$, where $a$ and $b$ are constants. What will be the mass of the isotope after $5$ years? Round your answer to the nearest tenth of a gram.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
