      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-45687",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/8f/8fcd5b1e9becdcda6b5c5f230cff04cf8e1961b175f379128059a2ba286d2437.png)\n\nA rumor is spreading through a town via social media. The number of people that know about the rumor can be modeled using the exponential function $P(t) = 2b^{t}$, where $b$ is a constant. The quantity $P$ is measured in thousands of people, and $t$ is the time, in hours, since the rumor started. How many people will know about the rumor after $4$ hours?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
